      <!-- Aligned vs GHYaf3-d1e838 (very heavily-abbreviated; the target d1e694 alone spanned 13
           source paragraphs). GHYaf3 split 36->74 so every target maps to at most one source, EXCEPT
           d1e300 (see below). Of 83 source paragraphs, 21 are dropped by the abbreviatio.
           *** NOTABLE: GHYaf3 (an abbreviatio by Henry Totting of Oyta) here ADDS content not in
           aw98wa (Wodeham): two GHYaf3 targets have NO sorb193 parallel - d1e398 ("Aliter respondet
           grego...") and d1e429 ("preceptum charitatis non obligat absolute...") - both citing/
           reasoning from "grego", almost certainly GREGORY OF RIMINI (Sent. lectures c.1343-44).
           Wodeham wrote BEFORE Gregory of Rimini, so he could not have cited him: this material can
           only be a post-Wodeham addition by Oyta, drawing on an authority that postdates his source.
           Verified by searching aw98wa for grego/contentari/"non obligat absolute" (no hits). So Oyta
           did not merely abridge Wodeham but supplemented him with a later authority.
           d1e300: the one un-splittable 1:many-source target - source d1e399 ("primo apparet") and
           d1e411 ("2o apparet") are compressed into a single sentence, so both assert to d1e300.
           SECOND-PASS CANDIDATES (source split across multiple targets; could be split source-side):
             d1e140 -> d1e150,159   d1e191 -> d1e178,185   d1e273 -> d1e215,229
             d1e357 -> d1e262,268   d1e371 -> d1e275,281   d1e1110 -> d1e486,502
             d1e1228 -> d1e530,534  d1e1484 -> d1e606,611  d1e1511 -> d1e657,674,694
             d1e2147 -> d1e1090,1140 -->
